From 82ed6c9ac4ead058b548fc1c3971ef6b715cbf5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Animesh Shaw <animeshshaw@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:51:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Update OWASP mapping to the LLM Top 10 2026 edition

The OWASP GenAI Security Project published the 2026 edition of the Top 10
for LLM Applications on 2026-08-03, superseding the 2025 list. Eight of the
ten entries changed rank and one was renamed, so the range's category labels
no longer match the current standard.

Remaps every category label to the 2026 edition:

  2025                              2026
  LLM01 Prompt Injection         -> LLM01 (steady)
  LLM02 Sensitive Info Disclosure-> LLM02 (steady)
  LLM03 Supply Chain             -> LLM04
  LLM04 Data and Model Poisoning -> LLM05
  LLM05 Improper Output Handling -> LLM10
  LLM06 Excessive Agency         -> LLM03
  LLM07 System Prompt Leakage    -> LLM08 Hidden Context Exposure (renamed)
  LLM08 Vector and Embedding     -> LLM09
  LLM09 Misinformation           -> LLM07
  LLM10 Unbounded Consumption    -> LLM06

Changes:
- owasp_notes.py: note blocks moved to their 2026 codes, with `code`/`num`
  updated to match. LLM08 renamed to Hidden Context Exposure and its copy
  broadened past the system prompt to any hidden context the model is given
  (retrieved policy text, tool schemas, workflow rules), per the 2026 scope.
- challenges/ and challenges/advanced/: `owasp` labels and module docstrings
  updated. Core and Advanced tiers both covered.
- live/scenarios/: The Report Renderer moves LLM05 -> LLM10.
- README, templates, app.py, card_svg.py, CONTRIBUTING.md: edition strings
  and both lab tables, reordered into 2026 rank order.

Deliberately unchanged:
- Challenge ids (`llm01`..`llm10`), module filenames, flags and solutions.enc.
  Solutions are keyed by challenge id and sealed under LLMVAULT_SOLUTION_KEY,
  which has no default, so renumbering ids here would break a store only you
  can regenerate.
- Registry ordering still sorts by id, so the lab grid now shows 2026 codes
  out of numeric order. Happy to add a sort-by-code change if you want it,
  but it changes UI behaviour so it seemed like a separate call.
- static/img/notes/*.png and docs/*.svg. Those are your artwork and excluded
  from the MIT grant by TRADEMARKS.md; icon_img paths stay pointed at the
  image for their category, so filenames no longer match their code.

Verified: all 20 Core + Advanced labs resolve to the correct note
(code and name agree); lab pages render the new labels. Test suite: 40 pass,
1 pre-existing failure in test_expert_unlock.py that also fails on an
unmodified checkout (the expert-vault audit logging in issue #2), untouched
here.
